# SocratiCode MCP — Primary Analysis Tool

Always prefer SocratiCode MCP tools over Grep, Glob, or SemanticSearch for code analysis.

## Tool Usage Map

| Task | SocratiCode Tool |
|------|-----------------|
| Find code by meaning/concept | `codebase_search` — semantic search across indexed codebase |
| Understand a function/class | `codebase_symbol` — definition + callers + callees in one call |
| Trace what code calls | `codebase_flow` — execution flow from an entry point |
| Impact of a change | `codebase_impact` — blast radius before refactoring/deleting |
| Search DB schema, API specs | `codebase_context_search` — context artifacts |
| Circular dependencies | `codebase_graph_circular` |
| Dependency graph stats | `codebase_graph_stats` |

## Required: Check Index Before Searching

Always call `codebase_status` first to confirm the index is ready.
If not indexed, call `codebase_index` with `projectPath: "c:\\Users\\Administrator\\Desktop\\ai-helper"`.

## projectPath

Always use: `c:\Users\Administrator\Desktop\ai-helper`

## Fallback Only

Use Grep/Read/Glob ONLY when:
- SocratiCode quota is exceeded (OpenAI error)
- Looking for an exact literal string (not semantic)
- Reading a specific known file line range
